            <ArticleTitle>[Diagnostic significance of protein complexes in ischemic and noncoronagenic damage of the myocardium].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>54-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A study of the structural aspects of blood serum albumin in patients with different forms of IHD and non-coronarogenous diseases of the myocardium revealed a reduction of spiralization of the albumin molecule, formation of modified form of protein and albumin-carbohydrate complexes. It is recommended to use these biochemical parameters in the complex diagnosis of different forms of cardiac pathology.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
